IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 220(c) to (h): the application to the Court of Chancery, the
-- burdens of proof, a director's right, and the limits on what the Court may order. Layer 1, from the text alone. Quote lines
-- are copied from de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script. The definitions and the stockholder's right and its conditions
-- ((a) and (b)) are in dg4-s220-inspection.l4.
--
-- The Court of Chancery is an official: no seat. Its powers are what a stockholder or director may ask for and what the
-- corporation is liable to; a judgment of the Court is an input, never guessed.
-- "5 business days" (c): the text does not define a business day and the core counts calendar time only, so the number of business
-- days that have passed is a plain input (fork F-B5; a business-day unit is listed under "Needs from the core").

§ `s 220 Inspection of books and records (c) to (h)`

§§ `s 220(c) The application to the Court of Chancery`

-- If the corporation, or an officer or agent of it, refuses to permit an inspection sought by a stockholder or by an attorney or
-- other agent acting for the stockholder under (b), or does not reply to the demand within 5 business days after the demand has
-- been made, the stockholder may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel the inspection. The Court has exclusive
-- jurisdiction to determine whether the person seeking inspection is entitled to the inspection sought.
-- src:875 | If the corporation, or an officer or agent thereof, refuses to permit an inspection sought by a stockholder or attorney or other agent acting for the stockholder pursuant to subsection (b) of this section or does not reply to the demand within 5 business days after the demand has been made, the stockholder may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel such inspection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875)
GIVEN `the corporation, or an officer or agent of it, refuses to permit an inspection sought under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has replied to the demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of business days after the demand was made that have ended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(c) the stockholder may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel the inspection` `the corporation, or an officer or agent of it, refuses to permit an inspection sought under subsection (b)` `the corporation has replied to the demand` `the number of business days after the demand was made that have ended` MEANS
        `the corporation, or an officer or agent of it, refuses to permit an inspection sought under subsection (b)`
    OR (    (NOT `the corporation has replied to the demand`)
        AND `the number of business days after the demand was made that have ended` AT LEAST 5)

-- src:875 | The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with exclusive jurisdiction to determine whether or not the person seeking inspection is entitled to the inspection sought. The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the stockholder to inspect the corporation’s stock ledger, an existing list of stockholders, and its other books and records, and to make copies or extracts therefrom; or the Court may order the corporation to furnish to the stockholder a list of its stockholders as of a specific date on condition that the stockholder first pay to the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing such list and on such other conditions as the Court deems appropriate. Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the corporation’s books and records, other than its stock ledger or list of stockholders, such stockholder shall first establish that:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875)
GIVEN `the action is brought in the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(c) the court has jurisdiction to determine whether the person seeking inspection is entitled to the inspection sought` `the action is brought in the Court of Chancery` MEANS
    `the action is brought in the Court of Chancery`

-- The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the stockholder to inspect the stock ledger, an existing list of
-- stockholders and its other books and records and to make copies or extracts; or may order the corporation to furnish a list of its
-- stockholders as of a specific date on condition that the stockholder first pay the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing the
-- list and on such other conditions as the Court deems appropriate. The Court may in its discretion prescribe limitations or
-- conditions on the inspection or award other or further relief, and may order books, documents and records, extracts or duly
-- authenticated copies to be brought within this State and kept here on the terms its order prescribes.
-- src:875 | The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the stockholder to inspect the corporation’s stock ledger, an existing list of stockholders, and its other books and records, and to make copies or extracts therefrom; or the Court may order the corporation to furnish to the stockholder a list of its stockholders as of a specific date on condition that the stockholder first pay to the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing such list and on such other conditions as the Court deems appropriate. …
-- src:879 | The Court may, in its discretion, prescribe any limitations or conditions with reference to the inspection, or award such other or further relief as the Court may deem just and proper. The Court may order books, documents and records, pertinent extracts therefrom, or duly authenticated copies thereof, to be brought within this State and kept in this State upon such terms and conditions as the order may prescribe.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875, 879)
DECLARE `s 220(c) Order the Court may make on a stockholder's application` IS ONE OF
    `a summary order that the corporation permit the stockholder to inspect the stock ledger, an existing list of stockholders and its other books and records and to make copies or extracts`
    `an order that the corporation furnish the stockholder a list of its stockholders as of a specific date`
    `a limitation or condition with reference to the inspection`
    `such other or further relief as the Court deems just and proper`
    `an order that books, documents and records, extracts or authenticated copies be brought within this State and kept in this State`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875, 879)
GIVEN order IS A `s 220(c) Order the Court may make on a stockholder's application`
      `the stockholder has applied under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(c) the Court of Chancery may make the order` order `the stockholder has applied under this subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `a summary order that the corporation permit the stockholder to inspect the stock ledger, an existing list of stockholders and its other books and records and to make copies or extracts` THEN `the stockholder has applied under this subsection`
    WHEN `an order that the corporation furnish the stockholder a list of its stockholders as of a specific date` THEN `the stockholder has applied under this subsection`
    WHEN `a limitation or condition with reference to the inspection` THEN `the stockholder has applied under this subsection`
    WHEN `such other or further relief as the Court deems just and proper` THEN `the stockholder has applied under this subsection`
    WHEN `an order that books, documents and records, extracts or authenticated copies be brought within this State and kept in this State` THEN `the stockholder has applied under this subsection`

-- An order that the corporation furnish a list of its stockholders as of a specific date is on condition that the stockholder first
-- pay the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing the list.
-- src:875 | or the Court may order the corporation to furnish to the stockholder a list of its stockholders as of a specific date on condition that the stockholder first pay to the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing such list and on such other conditions as the Court deems appropriate. Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the corporation’s books and records, other than its stock ledger or list of stockholders, such stockholder shall first establish that:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875)
GIVEN `the Court has ordered the corporation to furnish a list of its stockholders as of a specific date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(c) the stockholder must first pay the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing the list` `the Court has ordered the corporation to furnish a list of its stockholders as of a specific date` MEANS
    `the Court has ordered the corporation to furnish a list of its stockholders as of a specific date`

-- Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the books and records other than the stock ledger or list of stockholders, the stockholder
-- shall first establish (1) that the stockholder is a stockholder, (2) that the stockholder has complied with this section respecting
-- the form and manner of making demand, and (3) that the inspection sought is for a proper purpose.
-- src:875 | Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the corporation’s books and records, other than its stock ledger or list of stockholders, such stockholder shall first establish that:
-- src:876 | (1) Such stockholder is a stockholder;
-- src:877 | (2) Such stockholder has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand for inspection of such documents; and
-- src:878 | (3) The inspection such stockholder seeks is for a proper purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c)(1) to (3) (src:875-878)
GIVEN `the stockholder has established that the stockholder is a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has established that the stockholder has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has established that the inspection sought is for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(c) the stockholder has first established what the subsection requires for books and records other than the stock ledger and list of stockholders` `the stockholder has established that the stockholder is a stockholder` `the stockholder has established that the stockholder has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` `the stockholder has established that the inspection sought is for a proper purpose` MEANS
        `the stockholder has established that the stockholder is a stockholder`
    AND `the stockholder has established that the stockholder has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand`
    AND `the stockholder has established that the inspection sought is for a proper purpose`

-- Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the stock ledger or list of stockholders and establishes that the stockholder is a
-- stockholder and has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand, the burden of proof is on the
-- corporation to establish that the inspection sought is for an improper purpose. For other books and records the stockholder
-- carries the proper-purpose burden. If the stockholder has not yet established the two matters for the ledger or list, the text
-- does not say who bears the burden of purpose: NOTHING.
-- src:879 | Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the corporation’s stock ledger or list of stockholders and establishes that such stockholder is a stockholder and has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand for inspection of such documents, the burden of proof shall be upon the corporation to establish that the inspection such stockholder seeks is for an improper purpose. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:879)
GIVEN `the stockholder seeks to inspect the stock ledger or list of stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has established that the stockholder is a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has established that the stockholder has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Actor`
`s 220(c) the party who bears the burden of proof as to the purpose of the inspection` `the stockholder seeks to inspect the stock ledger or list of stockholders` `the stockholder has established that the stockholder is a stockholder` `the stockholder has established that the stockholder has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the stockholder seeks to inspect the stock ledger or list of stockholders`)
    THEN JUST `a stockholder`
    ELSE IF `the stockholder has established that the stockholder is a stockholder` AND `the stockholder has established that the stockholder has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand`
         THEN JUST `the corporation`
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 220(d) A director's right to examine`

-- Any director shall have the right to examine the corporation's stock ledger, a list of its stockholders, its books and records, and
-- other corporate records for a purpose reasonably related to the director's position as a director.
-- src:880 | Any director shall have the right to examine the corporation’s stock ledger, a list of its stockholders, its books and records, and other corporate records for a purpose reasonably related to the director’s position as a director. The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with the exclusive jurisdiction to determine whether a director is entitled to the inspection sought. The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the director to inspect the stock ledger, the list of stockholders, the books and records, and other corporate records and to make copies or extracts therefrom. The burden of proof shall be upon the corporation to establish that the inspection such director seeks is for an improper purpose. The Court may, in its discretion, prescribe any limitations or conditions with reference to the inspection, or award such other and further relief as the Court may deem just and proper.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(d) (src:880)
GIVEN `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is reasonably related to the director's position as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(d) the director has the right to examine the stock ledger, the list of stockholders, the books and records and other corporate records` `the person is a director` `the purpose is reasonably related to the director's position as a director` MEANS
        `the person is a director`
    AND `the purpose is reasonably related to the director's position as a director`

-- The Court of Chancery has exclusive jurisdiction to determine whether a director is entitled to the inspection sought, may
-- summarily order the corporation to permit it, and may prescribe limitations or conditions or award other relief. The burden of
-- proof is on the corporation to establish that the inspection the director seeks is for an improper purpose.
-- src:880 | The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with the exclusive jurisdiction to determine whether a director is entitled to the inspection sought. The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the director to inspect the stock ledger, the list of stockholders, the books and records, and other corporate records and to make copies or extracts therefrom. The burden of proof shall be upon the corporation to establish that the inspection such director seeks is for an improper purpose. The Court may, in its discretion, prescribe any limitations or conditions with reference to the inspection, or award such other and further relief as the Court may deem just and proper.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(d) (src:880)
DECLARE `s 220(d) Order the Court may make on a director's application` IS ONE OF
    `a summary order that the corporation permit the director to inspect the stock ledger, the list of stockholders, the books and records and other corporate records and to make copies or extracts`
    `a limitation or condition with reference to the inspection`
    `such other and further relief as the Court deems just and proper`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(d) (src:880)
GIVEN order IS A `s 220(d) Order the Court may make on a director's application`
      `the director has applied under this subsection to the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(d) the Court of Chancery may make the order` order `the director has applied under this subsection to the Court of Chancery` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `a summary order that the corporation permit the director to inspect the stock ledger, the list of stockholders, the books and records and other corporate records and to make copies or extracts` THEN `the director has applied under this subsection to the Court of Chancery`
    WHEN `a limitation or condition with reference to the inspection` THEN `the director has applied under this subsection to the Court of Chancery`
    WHEN `such other and further relief as the Court deems just and proper` THEN `the director has applied under this subsection to the Court of Chancery`

-- src:880 | The burden of proof shall be upon the corporation to establish that the inspection such director seeks is for an improper purpose. The Court may, in its discretion, prescribe any limitations or conditions with reference to the inspection, or award such other and further relief as the Court may deem just and proper.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(d) (src:880)
GIVETH A `Actor`
`s 220(d) the party who bears the burden of proof that the inspection the director seeks is for an improper purpose` MEANS
    `the corporation`

§§ `s 220(e) to (h) What more than the books and records the Court may order`

-- (e) Except as (f) or (g) expressly provides, in a proceeding by a stockholder under (c) to compel the inspection of books and
-- records, the Court may not order the corporation to produce any records other than the books and records set forth in
-- paragraph (a)(1). The stock ledger and the list of stockholders are not "books and records" as defined, and (c) itself
-- authorizes orders for them; (e) is read as limiting the orders about books and records (fork F-E2).
-- src:881 | (e) Except as otherwise expressly provided in subsection (f) or subsection (g) of this section, in any proceeding brought by a stockholder under subsection (c) of this section to compel the inspection of books and records, the Court of Chancery may not order the corporation to produce any records of the corporation other than the books and records set forth in paragraph (a)(1) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(e) (src:881)
GIVEN `the record is among the books and records set forth in paragraph (a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record is the stock ledger or a list of stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court may order the record produced under subsection (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court may order the record produced under subsection (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(e) the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce the record in a stockholder's proceeding` `the record is among the books and records set forth in paragraph (a)(1)` `the record is the stock ledger or a list of stockholders` `the Court may order the record produced under subsection (f)` `the Court may order the record produced under subsection (g)` MEANS
        `the record is among the books and records set forth in paragraph (a)(1)`
    OR  `the record is the stock ledger or a list of stockholders`
    OR  `the Court may order the record produced under subsection (f)`
    OR  `the Court may order the record produced under subsection (g)`

-- (f) If the corporation does not have any of the books and records described in (a)(1)c., e. or g. or, for a corporation with a
-- class of stock listed on a national securities exchange, (a)(1)i., the Court may order it to produce additional records
-- constituting the functional equivalent of them in response to a demand by a stockholder under (b) only if and to the extent the
-- stockholder has met the requirements of (b), and only to the extent necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder's proper
-- purpose. For a corporation whose stock is not listed, (f) does not reach paragraph (a)(1)i. (finding recorded in NOTES.md).
-- src:882 | (f) If the corporation does not have any of the books and records described in paragraph (a)(1)c., (a)(1)e., or (a)(1)g. of this section or, in the case of a corporation that has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange, paragraph (a)(1)i. of this section, the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce additional records of the corporation constituting the functional equivalent of any such books and records in response to a demand for inspection brought by a stockholder under subsection (b) of this section only if and to the extent the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b) of this section, and only to the extent necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder’s proper purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(f) (src:882)
GIVEN `the corporation does not have any of the books and records described in paragraphs (a)(1)c., e. or g.` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: listing on a national securities exchange (federal law; not among the inputs)
      `the corporation does not have the books and records described in paragraph (a)(1)i.` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are the functional equivalent of the books and records the corporation does not have` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder's proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(f) the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce the additional records constituting the functional equivalent` `the corporation does not have any of the books and records described in paragraphs (a)(1)c., e. or g.` `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange` `the corporation does not have the books and records described in paragraph (a)(1)i.` `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)` `the records are the functional equivalent of the books and records the corporation does not have` `the records are necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder's proper purpose` MEANS
        (   `the corporation does not have any of the books and records described in paragraphs (a)(1)c., e. or g.`
         OR (    `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange`
             AND `the corporation does not have the books and records described in paragraph (a)(1)i.`))
    AND `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)`
    AND `the records are the functional equivalent of the books and records the corporation does not have`
    AND `the records are necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder's proper purpose`

-- (g) The Court may order the corporation to produce other specific records only if and to the extent (1) the stockholder has met
-- the requirements of (b), (2) the stockholder has made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of the records to further
-- the stockholder's proper purpose, and (3) the stockholder has demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that the specific
-- records are necessary and essential to further that purpose.
-- src:883 | (g) In any proceeding brought by a stockholder under subsection (c) of this section to compel the inspection of books and records, the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce, in addition to any books and records or other records ordered to be produced under subsection (e) of this section, other specific records of the corporation only if and to the extent:
-- src:884 | (1) Such stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b) of this section;
-- src:885 | (2) Such stockholder has made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of such records to further the stockholder’s proper purpose; and
-- src:886 | (3) Such stockholder has demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that such specific records are necessary and essential to further such purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(g) (src:883-886)
GIVEN `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of the records to further the stockholder's proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that the specific records are necessary and essential to further that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 220(g) the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce the other specific records` `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)` `the stockholder has made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of the records to further the stockholder's proper purpose` `the stockholder has demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that the specific records are necessary and essential to further that purpose` MEANS
        `the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b)`
    AND `the stockholder has made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of the records to further the stockholder's proper purpose`
    AND `the stockholder has demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that the specific records are necessary and essential to further that purpose`

-- (h) The Court may impose reasonable restrictions as provided in (b)(3) on any records produced under (f) or (g). For records
-- produced otherwise the paragraph says nothing: NOTHING.
-- src:887 | (h) The Court of Chancery may impose reasonable restrictions as provided in paragraph (b)(3) of this section to any records of the corporation produced under subsection (f) or subsection (g) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(h) (src:887)
GIVEN `the records are produced under subsection (f) or subsection (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 220(h) the Court of Chancery may impose reasonable restrictions as provided in paragraph (b)(3) on the records` `the records are produced under subsection (f) or subsection (g)` MEANS
    IF `the records are produced under subsection (f) or subsection (g)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
